From ae65c57e5c6eae996c57c66192ad79279d3ada5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:48:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FUTEX-WAIT-ATOMIC1: the wait witness opens windows only with
 a peer running

At 9ce9845f the RISC-V wait witness spun out its first window: the waiter
held window B on CPU 1 with interrupts masked while its only signaller sat
queued behind it on the same CPU and init kept CPU 0, so no competing wake
could arrive before the QEMU timeout. The x86_64 and AArch64 runs, and a
pre-freeze RISC-V run, had landed the two threads on different CPUs.

The cell now runs two signallers (as FUTEX-REQUEUE-ATOMIC1's race witness
does) and init blocks on a futex instead of yielding while the witness
runs, and the kernel opens a witness wait's windows only while a sibling
thread of the waiter is current on another CPU; otherwise the wait is
logged FUTEX_WAIT_WITNESS_SKIPPED and runs unwindowed. The signallers'
stores share one counter, so every store writes a new value. The grader
excludes skipped waits from the window rules and still counts their
outcomes; self-test cases added. Witness builds only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLpmtT4bLN2gX3DCKAXYp8
